# ChatGPT Voice in India: PM Case Study

**Question:** How can ChatGPT mobile turn India's voice habit into higher-value voice usage?
NextLeap Product Management Fellowship, Milestones 1-3, by Harshvardhan Munda.

## 1. Context (M1: System Thinking)
- Indians already use voice everywhere (Google voice search, WhatsApp voice notes, YouTube, Alexa), but only about 10% of Indian AI users use voice mode (LocalCircles).
- Product gap: users don't know when voice is better (**discoverability**), can't verify or correct what was heard (**trust and control**), and voice isn't built for their language (**contextual relevance**).
- Voice KPI tree. North Star: successful voice-assisted tasks per eligible active user.

## 2. Segment and research (M2: User Research)
- **Chosen segment:** regional-language and Hinglish competitive-exam aspirants (UPSC, SSC, CAT, state exams). Big base, high typing pain, strong voice fit.
- **Survey:** 45 responses, 42 qualified. 40% never use voice or tried it once or twice.
- **Barriers (non-regular users, n=17):** accent or Hinglish misunderstanding 41%, typing is faster or more accurate 41%, concern about being overheard 35%.
- **Core problem:** a trust and control gap, not awareness. Users can't see, check or fix what voice captured, so they retype.

## 3. Solution (M3: Speak Your Way)
A UI-layer bundle on the existing voice stack. No new speech model.

| Feature | What it does |
|---|---|
| Language chip | Auto / Hinglish / Bangla + English / English, changeable mid-recording |
| Output toggle | Reply in same language / Hindi / Bangla / English, without a new query |
| Script choice | Roman or native script (Devanagari, Bengali) |
| Editable transcript | Tap any word to fix it before sending |
| Discovery nudge | One-time prompt near the mic, stops after 2 dismissals |

**Why this option:** scored highest on impact, confidence and ease (avg 7.7/10). A speech-model upgrade has the highest ceiling but the heaviest effort, so it's deferred.

## 4. Success metrics
| Stage | Metric | Target |
|---|---|---|
| North Star | Weekly voice queries per active aspirant | +30% vs baseline |
| Activation | First voice query within 7 days of nudge | 15% |
| Trust | Mixed-speech word error rate | under 10% |
| Retention | Week-4 voice repeat | 30% |
| Guardrails | Latency, cost, thumbs-up, dismissals | under 3s, within 20% of text cost |

## 5. Launch plan
Prototype tests (weeks 1-2), design (3), build and dogfood (4-6), A/B test on 10% of Hinglish and Bangla users on India Android (7-10), decision (11).

## 6. Decisions and open questions
- **Decided:** UI layer over model upgrade, Hinglish and Bangla first, separate input chip and output toggle.
- **Open:** does the UI layer alone move adoption, or is accuracy the real blocker? Which languages come next?

